{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 369 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the clindamycin phosphate injection shortage on 2023-03-21 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E42", "E37"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale East and Corvale Lakeside carries NDC 0781-3288-09 labeled by Sandoz Inc. and names InfoRLife SA as the manufacturing plant on the label.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E8", "E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected a registered plant for this supply chain, Bryant Ranch PrePack (FEI 1000519407), on 2022-03-17 and classified it VAI, with the classification letter dated 2022-05-19 — 369 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D8", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Subsequent inspections of that plant in 2023-06-16 and 2024-01-25 were also classified VAI, with classification letters issued after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D9", "D10", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Another registered plant, Pharmacia & Upjohn Company LLC (FEI 1810189), was inspected on 2023-06-16 and classified VAI, 87 days after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D9", "E35"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 6.2 days of the 6 mg/mL 50 mL bags on hand while Corvale Lakeside has 19.2 days and can spare 21 bags while retaining a two-week supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 21 bags from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East to 8 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D12"]
    }
  ]
}
